Nova Content Hub verified assistant runtime preflight
Date: 2026-10-19 Asia/Shanghai
Source: working tree based on d3172ac; coordinated release bump to 0.3.1 owned by parent agent.
This work did not build distribution packages, install/update host caches, modify host settings, disable hooks, alter hook timeouts, or commit.

Change:
- Extract snapshotPackage into shipped plugin-src/src/lib/package-snapshot.mjs; retain marketplace-builder import/reexport compatibility.
- Add stable descriptor reads with before/after identity checks, bounded streaming hashes, directory/link stability and no escaping links. Optional trusted expected entries reject unknown paths, size/mode/type/hash differences before execution.
- Add launchWithAssistantRuntime for explicit handoff launch only, after installed/enabled matching Skill verification. Readiness polling remains metadata-only.
- Read trusted app-bundled package-files.json through the existing bounded, ordinary-file, ancestor-no-symlink stable reader; require exact format/schema/full release.
- Compare the complete host-installed package tree with that trusted app inventory. Cache self-resealed integrity metadata never serves as the trust source.
- Only Codex may omit the absent node_modules/.bin/semver link when the trusted entry is exactly {link:../semver/bin/semver.js}. Existing modified links, all other omissions, and the same omission in WorkBuddy refuse.
- Capture Node/launcher file identities before full verification and recheck immediately before execFile. The exact verified host cache runtime/node (node.exe on Windows) runs fixed runtime/launch.mjs doctor; no shell, PATH search, app-copy fallback or cross-launch warm cache.
- Close stdin; 30-second timeout; SIGKILL on timeout; 64-KiB stdout/stderr buffers. Strip Node/Electron and loader injection environment variables, retaining ordinary PATH.
- Require successful exit, empty stderr and JSON ok:true/authMode:disabled/library:unbound/imageGeneration:false before creating the envelope or opening the assistant.
- Cover and template launch callbacks both await the same preflight. Errors preserve the existing fixed attempt and use existing NOT_READY recovery.

